{"include":["reasoning.encrypted_content"],"input":[{"content":"Work on src/solution.py using the provided tools. Read it before editing. Keep its public function names and call signatures. You may create and run Python checks under checks/; no tests are supplied. Python runs are read-only; use write_file for edits. Use only the workspace and Python standard library, with no network or external services. Finish with a brief summary. The final src/solution.py is your submitted implementation.","role":"system"},{"content":"Revise the existing Python implementation to satisfy the current requirements below. Treat these requirements as authoritative. Remove restrictions they do not require, preserve all specified functionality, and avoid unrelated changes. If no changes are needed, leave the implementation unchanged.\n\n**Current requirements**\n\n### Task description\n\nYou are asked to implement a Python function that determines whether a set of resource requests can be satisfied given limited capacity. The function takes as input a list of requests and available resources and returns whether a valid allocation exists. The goal is to determine feasibility of allocation based on the provided information. You may assume inputs are provided in a reasonable and consistent format. You may use ChatGPT to assist with reasoning about the problem, generating code, or writing tests.\n\nBriefly summarize any changes.\n","role":"user"},{"arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/solution.py\"}","call_id":"call_YlNZTvTKjlWgcmCDTcBv7wFs","id":"fc_045b439e4ec26364016aecf42f3dbc87d2b0a2de0bfc2d5573","name":"read_file","status":"completed","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"call_YlNZTvTKjlWgcmCDTcBv7wFs","output":"{\"content\":\"from typing import Dict, List, Union\\nfrom collections import defaultdict\\n\\nNumber = Union[int, float]\\n\\ndef is_allocation_feasible(\\n    resources: Dict[str, Number],\\n    requests: List[Dict[str, Number]]\\n) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Determine whether a set of resource requests can be satisfied given limited capacities.\\n\\n    Rules:\\n    - If a request references a resource not in `resources`, its capacity is treated as 0\\n      and the allocation fails (returns False).\\n    - Negative request amounts are not allowed.\\n    - Requests are indivisible.\\n    - Request order does not matter.\\n    - At least one resource must remain unallocated after task.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    # Validate resource capacities\\n    for r, cap in resources.items():\\n        if cap < 0:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Resource capacity for '{r}' must be non-negative\\\")\\n\\n    total_demand: Dict[str, Number] = defaultdict(float)\\n\\n    # Sum up all requests per resource\\n    for i, request in enumerate(requests):\\n        if not isinstance(request, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Request at index {i} must be a dictionary\\\")\\n\\n        for resource, amount in request.items():\\n            if not isinstance(amount, (int, float)):\\n                raise ValueError(\\n                    f\\\"Non-numeric request amount for resource '{resource}' in request index {i}\\\"\\n                )\\n\\n            if amount < 0:\\n                raise ValueError(\\n                    f\\\"Negative request amount for resource '{resource}' in request index {i}\\\"\\n                )\\n\\n            if resource not in resources:\\n                return False  # Requested resource does not exist\\n\\n            total_demand[resource] += amount\\n\\n    # Check if total demand exceeds capacities\\n    for resource, demand in total_demand.items():\\n        if demand > resources[resource]:\\n            return False\\n\\n    # Check the new requirement: at least one resource must remain unallocated\\n    for resource, capacity in resources.items():\\n        remaining = capacity - total_demand.get(resource, 0)\\n        if remaining > 0:\\n            return True  # At least one resource has leftover capacity\\n\\n    # All resources are fully consumed _ invalid allocation\\n    return False\",\"sha256\":\"cc5d7c26420678cea1e4419ae9cccfd1567750a79c5e05acc5425ae97556be09\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","type":"function_call_output"},{"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABq7PRFdB3jH-WMpYyfjxli7AD3avb3dRNIUpgHfkvGjjgF9mOptc0Rt5-okJ_flbvO9ePduFvwYmlo76V47Fa72yD6B7AsjJMwSovfpmLacYsBU_p4oIyE_eLfbye3eLtbdMF3CHH-yyPR7djwVdFf8ojJ8Qf5B2Z-qrDvEi1nVWc0f107Bq-BmiGaVHsiUe1BSJVW8C4h7Fj-9gX3SIYp0D-iLKu8uQn8EZNosDMWO_J4s7RYDhKMNtNQJu2gXwz4Fdf0r2_ev1YXEPWw0qYFbMgbKgBqGQaCGTEmw_6a0aJ8M_C0Rs4ky16zyl_KX3TxpXTp1RFbZbZTmKhTUFi9LXK_FDdbKc3zSOnFPtfcfzP0ni38ZJDeA56WPWdEh7g6pmNCO9SuOH4yE2a1QHnUnfc7vf57udkQ2NMQ-pOVsRtmo-36yXtG9wjFj1t9ROH5EUNG7oir_kaAY5KVZxy1f8ucYe6vQ91iz85HL4fu2CggRtnQ47Mn9uI2kgttGbAh9GDq_HFcCeHBviY6zK_UmA1pZ6CmnNwghUEJsEwbSbI46ufgv251132MHHyWO7WkiI8eAYc7w0KEEgnreHiiEzbZ1YIbv6KqyoGbtaZVeTxvftsMUMAeJJ1E6kqJo-EAvhuPTkxaBsjlmCZBMH4k_f3aQCAybZkh4KPpeqPEh_WY_gEru5RasPCuQXYHG5bbegRTi_qWeDanUkMj7485yI8_JMj6S-2N7tEEYxSb1I-7C70dgCAYboZYfdPjmX8PDWA_CIMIAXhqmPxFHRBErnenY7-Gzn_zaeAuVYtwn631ujYMnN6hyE5UEg8DbX5_nTG55D16vlj0kVD2cGXvtwaw5u0LdsWD1w3Y9Gyic_UjgThv2o1nHAjdj17jZBI6AGlGMToPS7k553-efstcH_FwTbtTbkg99vewvnb7ioM311PczD9sYoz5OZrZWDBo-4s8Fs8yqh-dQ-er0OE5tCVriEkqlHlDC9uaXY5sYmoHAKMi68QPni6rZzbJX6zWEXUTF8YBhV1qJO_tz8vdsubwrUXXF_VhJQjoG1RGO41rfSdqHojjXT5sFH50iSShxxHhGBGCKakqJGDEdaAtdUcjxFGZJRjMUEfn2BV9YwEQ-H7rYkgHRWGOqvXSnT3DOI_izHsR8EDL22barXwgPt5seyLtb1x_z1BkQTfFrQEn-nFUSbURlMOlQjnVjxQqtQdQQtUIBLgMA_Xo_5W5xHhoGFsiZJSzXdvjFTg9W4uXTXaWGW6Ub3_2zhRpGfQCBXEpvwzpGeVi7V7iafOmrHbgW09M1150ZpNO0Pc7rHpFkjqiBDi4TlzhxE1E8y0NIvw53PJSZGZglR7SirS16R5c6WYeGYUeiQw_PaI7Vd5n9v6A22whZ49l9GPiuq2nmmSaFY-OXkeeXvubIZPlH0hJGBDWYnC2GeseZbIq4rEVLQ0qK1sgrLtjiSl1RBJSSalwWPs1rojzt73DMgSjAGq0ofDDEA0ArfiNsK5dUp1Q2YAv9nrVM7ZOmHi7dFFcSDdnpGtT2cuHNW27oqdNynCSfmWNhQR8oxeA2TJnjzMJv9wOLf4mbglJVI4q9g99-jR0dHnNdalZaEOBsXIDDkvs5TbL68OaEOLMa6yeRTBReh9zKRxcZqlfvq3za5Y4RVaRlglfzGFksrpzufwbXQ9kIus0SJ_w69HfqpjR5gCgBDJafvhFXOwMy4ORvLRQ7lVEW05c